The instantiation of several R objects within one python process is
made impossible on purpose: R is not capable of multithreading
(and lot of the C code running R is probably not reentrant - unpredictable
things would happen).
I suspect that the choice of generating an error, rather than having a singleton
for that class for example, is to prevent accidental attempts at multithreading.

What could be tried is to spawn several python process, that would be
each importing the module "rpy".




