Message-ID: <B84DCBBE-58A0-447C-BDC5-41A51DC25591@mac.com>

During the installation of R, there is an option (on by default) to  
set the R registry entries.  If, for some reason, this gets  
unchecked, it doesn't happen.

In any case, the problem can be solved by properly setting the RHOME  
environment variable.  The RHOME environment variable should point to  
the root of the R installation path, as reported by executing the  
command

	/path/to/the/executable/R.exe RHOME

-Greg



