2008/1/29, Toby Hocking <THocking at sangamo.com>:
> These new slice changes are breaking my rpy compilation:
>
> gcc -pthread -fno-strict-aliasing -g -Wall -fPIC -DWITH_NUMERIC=1 -DRPY_SHNAME=_rpy2021 -DINIT_RPY=init_rpy2021 -UPRE_2_2 -I/usr/lib/R/include -Isrc -I/usr/share/R/include -I/usr/include/python2.4 -c src/rpymodule2021.c -o build/temp.linux-i686-2.4/src/rpymodule2021.o -shared
>
> src/rpymodule2021.c:1556: error: 'ssizeargfunc' undeclared here (not in a function)
>
> src/rpymodule2021.c:1556: error: expected '}' before 'Robj_item'
>
> error: command 'gcc' failed with exit status 1
>
> Maybe I need some additional development libraries??? Which ones?

Python 2.5.

I did revert the use of type Py_ssize_t I had for my local copy,
but forget ssizes elsewhere.

I think that ssizeargfunc (and ssizessizeargfunc) were probably not yet around
in Python 2.4. Replacing them with intargfunc (and intintargfunc respectively)
should make it python 2.4-friendly (although generate deprecation warnings
with 2.5).
I'll fix it later on today.

Thanks,


Laurent



